    <title>Do Language Models Understand
  Language? A Benchmark Study</title>
    <summary>  We evaluate whether large language models understand language by testing them on
  compositional generalization tasks. Results show strong performance on in-distribution
  data. However, models fail systematically on novel compositions, suggesting that
  surface statistics rather than understanding drive their behavior.
</summary>
    <author><name>Ada  Lovelace</name></author>
